  "_notes": [
    "CLR leads its group because nothing PROVEN overhead is UNTESTED — not thin, and not absent either; the group's position is HIS CALL (band_structure.CEILING_GROUP_UNTESTED) and the shipped default is kept.",
    "TIE_B beats TIE_A on an identical ceiling and an identical gap because its first support band is the bigger one — the last tiebreak, and the only place ask #2's 'bands are bigger' can decide.",
    "NOSEC has one support band and no second: its gap is UNKNOWN, never 0, so it sorts behind every row that has a second catch rather than ahead of them.",
    "UNKC has a floor but no readable ceiling — it sorts behind every readable ceiling, because unknown is not thin.",
    "NA is a tab with no band read and NONE has no read at all: both last, never first.",
    "STRH carries height_pct as the STRING \"5.0\": the backend coerces it and ranks it beside TIE_A. A side that treats a string as unreadable drops it into the unknown-ceiling group instead — which is the divergence this row exists to catch.",
    "TRUTHY carries applicable = 1, not true. The backend reads it as applicable and it LEADS the fallback board (a second catch 1% under). A side that tests `applicable !== true` sends it to the very last place — as far apart as two answers can be.",
    "AB / A_B / aB have identical reads and differ only by symbol: the order is Python codepoint order, '_' (0x5F) after 'B' and uppercase before lowercase. A locale collation reorders all three."
  ]
